FUNDAMENTALS (Transformer Attention)

Types / matrices:
  Q : Query     — what is being sought
  K : Key       — what is available to be matched
  V : Value     — the content that gets retrieved / shared

Scaled dot-product attention:
  scores     = (Q @ K.T) / sqrt(d_k)
  weights    = softmax(scores)
  output     = weights @ V

Softmax:
  softmax(x)_i = exp(x_i) / sum_j exp(x_j)
  Turns raw similarity into a probability distribution over a finite attention budget.

d_k : key dimension (scale factor so dots don't explode)
attention budget : finite; mass must sum to ~1

